  "summary": "@newspage/libx-amount exfiltrates host/user identifiers to external endpoint on require",
  "details": "On module load, the package reads the HOSTNAME/COMPUTERNAME and USER/USERNAME environment variables, hex-encodes them, and transmits them as a query parameter via https.get to the hardcoded host accenture-npm.azurewebsites.net (path /libx?h=<hex>). The package ships placeholder metadata (description 'A simple placeholder for npm.', author 'anonymous', version 99.99.42) and a scoped name resembling an internal organization package — the shape of a dependency-confusion squat whose only effect on install is to beacon installer identity to an external endpoint.",
